./clean-ci.sh
./deploy-ci.sh
create jenkins user with jenkins db
create creds for jenkins and rabbtmq 
ci-firewall toolkit sendq create --amqpuri amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672/

in jenkins/Systems/CI Monitor add rabbitmq provider
h:rabbitmq
5672
vh:/
amqp.ci.exchange.send
amqp.ci.topic.send
amqp.ci.queue.send

crete jenkins project
add ci trigger with rabbitmq
enable concurrent builds
Also insert AMQP_URI as arg ie 
AMQP_URI=amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672/
on sender
on recever set it to 
AMQP_URI=amqp://guest:guest@rabbitmq:5672/ 

In jenkins add it as a secret text env
Do same for jenkins robot account ie
JENKINS_URL=http://jenkins:8080
JENKINS_ROBOT_USER=jenkins
JENKINS_ROBOT_PASSWORD=jenkins
DOnt forget to update system setting jenkins advertised url to same

in exec shell put:
```
rm -rf ./*
curl -kJLO https://github.com/mohammedzee1000/ci-firewall/releases/download/v0.1.3/ci-firewall-linux-amd64.tar.gz
tar -xzf ./ci-firewall-linux-amd64.tar.gz && rm -rf ./ci-firewall-linux-amd64.tar.gz && chmod +x ./ci-firewall
script --return -c "./ci-firewall work --env 'FOO1=BAR1' --env 'FOO2=BAR2'" /dev/null
rm -rf ./*
```

